\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Why a sample is deleted, and what the deletion did.} (a)~One end-to-end latency of $0.35$~ms, starting at four phases within one millisecond. Three finish inside it, compute to $0$~ms and are deleted. The fourth crosses a millisecond boundary, one of the \emph  {grid} instants at which the clock's digit changes, and is kept, as exactly $1$~ms. (b)~Each of the $75$ settings with a captured summary, at the median the benchmark printed and its retention. $71$ settings print $1.0$ or $2.0$~ms while retention spans $279\times $. Above the grid, nothing is lost only at $256$~KB.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:deletion}{{3}{7}{\textbf {Why a sample is deleted, and what the deletion did.} (a)~One end-to-end latency of $0.35$~ms, starting at four phases within one millisecond. Three finish inside it, compute to $0$~ms and are deleted. The fourth crosses a millisecond boundary, one of the \emph {grid} instants at which the clock's digit changes, and is kept, as exactly $1$~ms. (b)~Each of the $\ombMedianCells $ settings with a captured summary, at the median the benchmark printed and its retention. $\ombGridMedianCells $ settings print $\ombGridPrintedLo $ or $\ombGridPrintedHi $~ms while retention spans $\ombRetentionFold \times $. Above the grid, nothing is lost only at $\ombAboveGridWholeKB $~KB}{figure.3}{}}
